**GROUP FOUR - TASK III (10 Marks)**

The **Body Mass Index (BMI)** is a value derived from the mass (weight) and height of an individual, male or female.

Note the following:

- BMI = (mass or weight)/(height*height) expressed in units of Kg/m$^2$,
- height is in meters
- mass or weight is in Kg

**C program**

```c
#include<stdio.h>
int main() {
  float w, h, bmi;
  printf("Enter height in metres: ");
  scanf("%f", &h);
  printf("Enter weight in kilograms: ");
  scanf("%f", &w);
  bmi = w/(h*h);
  printf("\nBody Mass Index: %.2f\n", bmi);
  getchar();
}
```

**Pascal program**

```pascal
Program BMIndex;
Var
  w, h, bmi : real;
Begin
  write('Enter height in metres: ');
  readln(h);
  write ('Enter weight in kilograms: ');
  readln(w);
  bmi := w/(h*h);
  writeln;
  writeln ('Body Mass Index: ', bmi:0:2);
  readln();
End.
```
